<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela oil workers kidnapped on Colombia border.</title>
<headline>Venezuela oil workers kidnapped on Colombia border.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two Venezuelan oil engineers were kidnapped on Wednesday by &quot;presumed guerrilla groups&quot; near the Colombian border.</p>
<p>The two workers were snatched from oil fields in the Victoria zone of the southwestern state of Apure and taken into Colombian territory, a spokesman for Corpoven said. The company is a subsidiary of state-owned oil company Petroleos de Venezuela.</p>
<p>&quot;On Wednesday, in the afternoon, two company employees were kidnapped and taken to Colombian territory by presumed guerrilla groups working on the border,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Corpoven was pursuing all avenues with military and civilian authorities to protect the safety of the hostages and obtain their release, he added.</p>
</text>
